// apue client runtime for Java 17+ (JDK standard library only: java.net.http.HttpClient, HTTP/2 over
// TLS with HTTP/1.1 fallback). Embedded into every file generated by `apue-types --lang java`: the
// generator takes the imports and everything between the runtime markers and nests it in the
// generated class, next to the API's types and a Client with one method per op. Compiles on its own.
// A client is thread-safe (one HttpClient, multiplexed HTTP/2 connection, no mutable state).
// Covers: unary calls (GET ?i= with canonical JSON for cacheable reads, POST otherwise,
// Idempotency-Key for non-safe calls), retries for safe and keyed calls (connection loss, 429/503
// honouring Retry-After, 409 with retryable: true), server streams (closeable early), client and bidi
// streams (half duplex: JDK 17's HttpClient exposes the response only after the request body is
// complete), RFC 9457 problems incl. END-frame errors, deadlines, bytes in messages (BLOB frames,
// $blob/$lit), uploads for bytes/file inputs (one request each, not resumed; deleted after the call),
// t.download() outputs (resumed with Range + If-Range, SHA-256 verified).
// Not covered: resuming broken streams, batches, full duplex, compression, client-side validation.

